course: dictionary
lesson: 12276
title: Telling things apart with contradistinction
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Contradistinction is a formal noun. It means showing how two things are different by setting them side by side as opposites. You will almost always meet it in the phrase «in contradistinction to», which means «as opposed to» or «unlike».
explain: «In contradistinction to the cat, the dog loves to fetch.» The sentence puts a dog next to a cat and says they are different. The clue is the word «in contradistinction to», which tells you the dog is the opposite of the cat in this way.
explain: This is a stiff, formal phrase, so you will mostly see it in books, essays and exam texts. In your own writing, «unlike» or «in contrast to» is clearer and easier for your reader to follow.
fact: Contradistinction means showing how two things are different, by setting them against each other.
fact: The phrase «in contradistinction to» means «as opposed to» or «unlike».
fact: «In contradistinction to summer, winter is cold.» Here winter is set against summer as the opposite.
fact: In your own writing, «unlike» or «in contrast to» is clearer than «in contradistinction to».
exercise: «In contradistinction to the cat, the dog loves to fetch.» What does in contradistinction to mean here? | *As opposed to, unlike the cat | Exactly the same as the cat | Before the cat arrived | Chasing after the cat
exercise: Which word could replace «in contradistinction to» in «In contradistinction to summer, winter is cold»? | because of | *unlike | during | like
exercise: Ava wants to write clearly for her teacher. Which phrase should she use instead of contradistinction? | in the middle of | *in contrast to | in a hurry | in the same way
test: «Tom is loud, in contradistinction to his quiet brother.» What does this sentence show? | Tom is talking to his brother | *Tom and his brother are different | Tom is quieter than his brother | Tom and his brother are exactly the same
test: Which phrase means the same as «in contradistinction to»? | as a result of | in order to | at the same time as | *as opposed to
exam: «Cats hunt at night, in contradistinction to most birds, which sing at dawn.» What does the sentence show? | *Cats and birds are different in when they are active | Cats and birds are alike in when they are active | Birds hunt at night, like cats | Cats sing at dawn, like birds
